{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-190869-r4513973","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Boliche (Cuban Chorizo-Stuffed Roast)","sourcePageId":190869,"sourceRevision":"4513973","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-19T01:42:31Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Boliche%20(Cuban%20Chorizo-Stuffed%20Roast)&oldid=4513973","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:24:45.135Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Cuban recipes","Category:Main course recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using beef round","Category:Recipes using caper","Category:Recipes using chorizo","Category:Recipes using cilantro","Category:Recipes using garlic","Category:Recipes using green bell pepper","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Roasted recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"04537436bd494b3ace850ca201bb513c7cd18e5701f8bb4ce487969d677046fa","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Beef recipes\n| Servings = 6–8\n| Image = [[File: Boliche.jpg|300px]]\n}}\n\n{{recipe|date=November 2008}}\n\n'''Boliche''' (pronounced bow-'''lee'''-chay) is a popular Cuban dish consisting of eye round roast stuffed with chorizo sausages simmered in a tomato sauce base.\n== Ingredients ==\n*3–5 [[Cookbook:Pound|lb]] [[Cookbook:Beef|beef]] eye round roast\n*4 Goya [[Cookbook:Chorizo|chorizos]], quartered lengthwise\n*2 tbsp Goya adobo seasoning\n*2 large [[Cookbook:Pinch|pinches]] [[Cookbook:Saffron|saffron]]\n*6 cloves [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]], [[Cookbook:Mince|minced]]\n*1 large [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n*1 large green [[Cookbook:Bell Pepper|bell pepper]]\n*3 [[Cookbook:Bay Leaf|bay leaves]]\n*1–2 heaping tbsp [[Cookbook:Oregano|oregano]]\n*3 tbsp green Spanish [[Cookbook:Olive|olives]] with [[Cookbook:Pimento|pimentos]]\n*3 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Caper|capers]]\n*2 packets Goya sazon con azafran\n*1 cup [[Cookbook:Red Wine|red wine]]\n*1 can (29 oz) [[Cookbook:Tomato Sauce|tomato sauce]]\n*¼ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Olive Oil|olive oil]]\n*1 package Badia [[Cookbook:Cilantro|cilantro]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n# Cut slits into eye round roast, and stuff with quartered chorizos (follow the grain of meat).\n# Lightly rub meat with adobo seasoning.\n# Brown the meat on all sides in a [[Cookbook:Sauté Pan|sauté pan]] to seal in the juices. Remove and place in a large covered roasting pan.\n# In the same pan as the beef was browned, add saffron, garlic, onions, peppers, bay leaves, oregano, olives, capers, and the Sazon seasoning. [[Cookbook:Sautéing|Sauté]] until the onions are translucent in color. \n# [[Cookbook:Deglazing|Deglaze]] with red wine, turn heat down, and [[Cookbook:Simmering|simmer]] about 5 minutes. Add the cilantro and the tomato sauce and stir well. \n# Pour this mixture over the beef, and [[Cookbook:Roasting|roast]] at 325 °F for 1 ½–2 hours, or until meat is tender. Turn the roast over and [[Cookbook:Basting|baste]] with the sauce once in a while to assure full flavor penetration and even cooking.\n# Serve.\n\n[[Category:Cuban recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using beef round]]\n[[Category:Recipes using caper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chorizo]]\n[[Category:Roasted recipes]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using green bell pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cilantro]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Boliche (Cuban Chorizo-Stuffed Roast)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"6–8","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"3–5 lb beef eye round roast","sourceText":"3–5 lb beef eye round roast","amountText":"3–5 lb beef eye round roast","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"4 Goya chorizos, quartered lengthwise","sourceText":"4 Goya chorizos, quartered lengthwise","amountText":"4 Goya chorizos, quartered lengthwise","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"2 tbsp Goya adobo seasoning","sourceText":"2 tbsp Goya adobo seasoning","amountText":"2 tbsp Goya adobo seasoning","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"2 large pinches saffron","sourceText":"2 large pinches saffron","amountText":"2 large pinches saffron","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"6 cloves garlic, minced","sourceText":"6 cloves garlic, minced","amountText":"6 cloves garlic, minced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1 large onion, chopped","sourceText":"1 large onion, chopped","amountText":"1 large onion, chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"1 large green bell pepper","sourceText":"1 large green bell pepper","amountText":"1 large green bell pepper","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"3 bay leaves","sourceText":"3 bay leaves","amountText":"3 bay leaves","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"1–2 heaping tbsp oregano","sourceText":"1–2 heaping tbsp oregano","amountText":"1–2 heaping tbsp oregano","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-10","name":"3 tbsp green Spanish ol